%I A402453 #10 Nov 18 2026 22:31:50
%S A402453 21,35,39,40,55,56,57,63,65,68,77,80,85,87,88,95,102,104,105,112,117,
%T A402453 132,136,141,143,147,148,152,155,160,165,168,171,175,176,177,185,187,
%U A402453 189,190,195,200,201,204,205,208,209,220,224,231,232,237,245,248,255,260,261
%N A402453 Numbers k such that the minimal element of some coset of (Z/kZ)*^2 in (Z/kZ)* is composite, where (Z/kZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo k and (Z/kZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402453 In other words, k is a term if and only if: There exists m coprime to k, not a square modulo k, such that m/p is not a square modulo k for every prime p <= m not dividing k.
%C A402453 All terms belong to A033949. Complement of A402452 in A033949.
%C A402453 If k = p^e*s for p odd prime, e >= 2, and gcd(p,s) = 1, since squares modulo n and squares modulo p*s are the same, k is a term if and only if p*s is. Similarly, if k = 2^e*s for e >= 4 and odd s, k is a term if and only if 8*s is.
%C A402453 The k-th row of A402418 lists the minimal elements of cosets of (Z/kZ)*^2 in (Z/kZ)*.
%H A402453 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402453/b402453.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A402453 21 is a term: For m = 10 (a coprime nonsquare modulo 21), there exists no prime p < 10 not dividing 21 such that 10/p is a square modulo 21, since 10/2 and 10/5 are nonsquares modulo 21.
%e A402453 35 is a term: For m = 6 (a coprime nonsquare modulo 35), there exists no prime p < 6 not dividing 35 such that 35/p is a square modulo 35, since 6/2 and 6/3 are nonsquares modulo 35.
%e A402453 102 is a term: For m = 35 (a coprime nonsquare modulo 102), there exists no prime p < 35 not dividing 102 such that 35/p is a square modulo 102, since 35/5, 35/7, 35/11, 35/13, 35/19, 35/23, 35/29, and 35/31 are nonsquares modulo 102.
%e A402453 840 is a term: For m = 187 (a coprime nonsquare modulo 840), there exists no prime p < 187 not dividing 840 such that 840/p is a square modulo 840, since 187/11, 187/13, ..., 187/181 are nonsquares modulo 840.
%o A402453 (PARI) isA402453(n) = !isA402452(n, 0) \\ see A402452 for its program
%Y A402453 Cf. A033949, A402418, A402452.
%K A402453 nonn,new
%O A402453 1,1
